---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for CortexFlow — what data we collect, how we use it, cookies, advertising, and your rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="prose-wrap">
    <section class="section prose">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p>
      <p class="kicker">CORTEXFLOW · FREE FOREVER</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--muted);">Last updated: October 2, 2026</p>

      <p>
        CortexFlow ("we", "us", "our") runs the website at
        <a href="https://cortexflow.tech">cortexflow.tech</a>. This policy explains
        what information we collect when you visit, and how we use it. The short
        version: we collect as little as possible, we don't sell your data, and
        accounts are optional and free — they're only needed to download
        workflow templates. Reading articles needs no account.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you give us.</strong> If you email us, we receive
          your name, email address, and message. We use it only to reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter.</strong> If you subscribe to the newsletter, we
          store your email address and signup date on our own infrastructure
          (Cloudflare KV — no third-party email service). We use it only to
          send you new-post notifications. Every email includes an unsubscribe
          link, and unsubscribing permanently deletes your address. We never
          sell or share your email.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account.</strong> If you create a free account (needed to
          download workflow templates), sign-in is handled by Firebase
          Authentication (Google). If you sign up with an email address, your
          password is stored by Firebase and never touches our servers; if you
          sign in with Google, Google handles the login. We store only your
          profile — name, email address, sign-in provider, account creation
          date, and last login — in Firebase Firestore (Google's database),
          under your own user record. When you sign in, we set a secure
          session cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, 30-day expiry) so the
          site remembers you're logged in; signing out deletes it. Password
          resets and verification emails are sent to your email address by
          Firebase. You can delete your account anytime by emailing
          hello@cortexflow.tech — deletion removes your profile, sessions, and
          all account data permanently. We never sell or share your account
          data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical information.</strong> Our hosting provider
          (Cloudflare) may process standard web-server data — such as your IP
          address, browser type, and pages visited — to keep the site secure,
          fast, and reliable. We don't use this to identify you personally.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Essential.</strong> If you sign in, we set one session cookie to
        keep you logged in. It holds only a session token, expires after 30
        days, and is removed when you sign out.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how
        visitors use the site (pages visited, approximate location, device
        type). Google Analytics sets cookies to collect this data on Google's
        behalf; we don't use it to identify you personally. You can opt out
        with Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Advertising.</strong> We run Google AdSense (Auto ads).
        Google and its partners may use cookies — including the Google
        DoubleClick cookie — to serve ads based on your visits to this and
        other sites. You can opt out of personalized advertising at
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google's Ads Settings</a>.
        Our <a href="/ads.txt">ads.txt</a> lists the sellers authorized to sell
        our ad inventory.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some articles on this site contain affiliate links to third-party tools
        and services. If you click one and make a purchase, we may earn a
        commission at no extra cost to you. The merchant — not us — may set a
        cookie to track the referral. Their privacy policies apply to that data.
      </p>

      <h2>4. External links</h2>
      <p>
        Our tutorials link to third-party documentation, tools, and communities.
        We aren't responsible for the privacy practices of those sites; please
        review their policies before sharing personal information with them.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is aimed at adult builders and isn't directed at children
        under 13. We don't knowingly collect information from children.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site evolves. The "Last updated" date
        at the top will always reflect the latest version.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.authorEmail}`}>{SITE.authorEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
